Where the full texts are
------------------------

In the app, Malini.app/Contents/Resources holds LICENSE, this NOTICE,
LICENSE.electron.txt (Electron) and LICENSES.chromium.html (Chromium, Node.js
and every library they include).
Each bundle in app.asar (out/main, out/renderer) carries THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt
with the full license text of every npm package in that bundle, generated at
build time by apps/malini/scripts/third-party-notices.mjs.
The agent bridge in Resources/agent-bridge/node_modules keeps each package's own
license file, and Resources/vendor/gh keeps the GitHub CLI's LICENSE.
In the source, the sounds' licenses are in apps/malini/src/renderer/public/sounds
and the file icons' license is in apps/malini/src/renderer/public/file-icons/LICENSE.
The standard license texts named below are at https://spdx.org/licenses/.

